      "question_type": "mcq",
      "rationale": "They keep wall forms from spreading under the fluid pressure of newly placed concrete. The audited sources support formwork components, fresh-concrete pressure, scaffolding access, and shoring as temporary support.",
      "explanation": "Steel panels are system formwork, more expensive. Aluminum/OSB is less common in Philippine practice; coco lumber dominates. Plastic formwork is rare; timber is cost-effective. Conventional formwork: timber beams (coco lumber is economical in Philippines)/joists → plywood decking → props (vertical timber or steel columns) at base. Advantages: flexible, adaptable, low capital cost, reusable ~5–10 times. Standard in Philippine low-rise construction.",
      "code_citation": "ACI 347R-14; Philippine construction practice",
